{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"DIAGNOSTIC STATE — plan PASSED first round (0 blocking, 1 advisory), SIGNED at 44d9250ea, CLAIMED. Recording the trace so far so the next session starts from data, not from scratch.\n\n**BOTH HALVES OF THE PLUMBING LOOK CORRECT IN ISOLATION — that is the puzzle, and it is why the plan forbids assuming the `gate_config` omission is the cause.**\n* AGENT steps: `workflow/runs.py:144-156` `RunnerAgentStep.run` does\n    cfg = self._config or LLMConfig.from_env(repo_root=self._repo_root)\n    cfg = replace(cfg, model=resolve_model(cfg, step=ctx.step.get('model'), workflow=ctx.workflow.get('model')))\n  and the code-review dispatch DOES pass `config=cfg` into `RunnerAgentStep`. So a prompt step's\n  `model:` is read and resolved — on this path.\n* BATCH steps: `code_review/batch_runner.py:60-61,83-84` resolves `req.model_ladder[0]` via\n  `resolve_model_string` and sets `step['model'] = model`. Also correct — on this path.\n* The doc is NOT transformed: `_assemble_code_review_run` does a plain `doc = _gate_doc(\"code-review\", repo_root)`, and the package demonstrably loads the worktree file with all five declarations.\n\n**WHY THE LIVE LOG CANNOT SETTLE WHICH PATH RAN — a real limitation of the instrument.** `usage_log.record(op=...)` records the PROMPT NAME, not the step id. `code-review-base` is the prompt used BOTH by the `base` step AND as the `batch:` finder for `round_a`/`round_b`, so the nine observed ops cannot be attributed to steps. `code-review-docs` / `-tests` / `-deletion-impact` / `-project-review-phase-boundaries` / `-api-compat` are criteria overlays, i.e. batch work; `code-review-verify` and `code-review-coach` look like agent steps. But 'looks like' is not attribution, and attributing them by name would repeat the reasoning error that has already cost this epic three false starts.\n\n**THEREFORE THE RECORDING-RUNNER TEST IS THE DIAGNOSTIC, NOT JUST THE REGRESSION GUARD.** It observes (step_id -> model handed to the runner) directly, which is the one fact neither the usage log nor source reading has produced. Write it FIRST, confirm RED, and let it name the broken seam — then fix exactly that.\n\nCONFIRMED FACTS to build on (all independently verified): the defect is real and pre-existing (nine calls all on `cfg.model`, including `verify`'s 172e-era `model: standard`); H2 (config not loaded) and H3 (class table falling back to built-in defaults) are both ELIMINATED — H3 because `_DEFAULT_MODEL_BY_CLASS['standard']` is sonnet and `verify` ran on OPUS; and the asymmetry lead stands — plan-review wraps `gate_config(cfg)` (gate_dispatch ~:146-163) and code-review does not (~:414-424), while plan-review demonstrably honours classes (41/1 opus/sonnet observed live across two providers)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785608809857593001,"uuid":"65f07bfb-f8b3-49b7-b2c9-dd5b2a369f24"}